<header><p class="st-kicker">kingdom · British Isles</p><h1 class="st-title">Kingdom of Fermanagh</h1><p class="st-meta">1264 CE – 1607 CE (approx.) · capital Enniskillen</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">The Maguire lordship around Lough Erne, a Gaelic lordship of islands and churches whose last chief joined the Flight of the Earls.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/maguire-dynasty">Maguires</a> rose in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/county-fermanagh">Fermanagh</a> in the 13th century, with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/donn-carrach-maguire">Donn Carrach Maguire</a>, who died in 1302, counted as their first king from about 1264. They displaced earlier rulers and became <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vassal">vassals</a> of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/o-neill-dynasty">O'Neills</a> of the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/kingdom-of-tir-eoghain">Kingdom of Tir Eoghain</a>.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/county-fermanagh">Fermanagh</a> was organised around <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lough-erne">Lough Erne</a>, with islands, crannogs and monasteries such as <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/devenish-island">Devenish</a>. The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/maguire-dynasty">Maguires</a> built <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/enniskillen-castle">Enniskillen Castle</a> in the 15th century. Their learned families compiled the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/annals-of-ulster">Annals of Ulster</a> on <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/belle-isle-fermanagh">Belle Isle</a> under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cathal-mac-maghnusa">Cathal Mac Maghnusa</a>. Their economy rested on <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cattle">cattle</a> and fishing.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hugh-maguire-lord-of-fermanagh">Hugh Maguire</a> fought with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hugh-oneill-earl-of-tyrone">Hugh O'Neill</a> in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nine-years-war-ireland">Nine Years' War</a> and died in 1600. His brother <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cu-chonnacht-maguire">Cuchonnacht</a> left with the Flight of the Earls in 1607. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/county-fermanagh">Fermanagh</a> was then planted with English and Scottish settlers, and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/enniskillen">Enniskillen</a> became a Protestant garrison town.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/kingdom-of-fermanagh.jpg" alt="Kingdom of Fermanagh" width="320" height="267"><figcaption>Image: Mabuska · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Ulster_Early_16th_Century.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1264 CE – 1607 CE (approx.)</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/13th-century">13th century</a> – <a href="/centuries/17th-century">17th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>kingdom</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>feudal</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Enniskillen</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Donn Carrach Maguire, Hugh Maguire, Cuchonnacht Maguire</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Christianity</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Irish</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/united-kingdom">United Kingdom</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Fir Manach, Maguire's Country</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1436&amp;focus=kingdom-of-fermanagh" aria-label="Kingdom of Fermanagh on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="4511 315 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Kingdom of Fermanagh lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M4831 571L4851 567M4831 571L4861 599"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M4851 567h0M4861 599h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M4831 571h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M4831 571h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks Enniskillen. <a href="/atlas?year=1436&amp;focus=kingdom-of-fermanagh">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>

